      "title": "H3 edit prompt | <Picture 1>, <Picture 2>",
      "properties": {
        "cnr_id": "comfy-core",
        "ver": "0.45.0",
        "Node name for S&R": "MiniMaxH3ImageConditioning"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "Edit <Picture 1>. Keep the person EXACTLY the same individual, but dress them in the complete outfit from <Picture 2>.\n\nUse <Picture 1> for the person's facial identity, skin, hair, body shape, original pose, hands, environment and camera composition. Use <Picture 2> ONLY for garments, clothing layers, colors, fabric, materials, patterns, fit and clothing-related accessories.\n\nTransfer the distinctive wardrobe from <Picture 2> accurately rather than inventing an unrelated outfit.\n\nIMPORTANT: Replace the entire visible outfit, not just the upper-body clothing. Transfer all corresponding garments from <Picture 2>, including shirts, tops, sweaters, jackets, coats, pants, jeans, trousers, skirts, dresses, footwear, hats, belts and other clothing accessories when present.\n\nPay particular attention to lower-body clothing. If pants, jeans, skirts or other lower-body garments are visible in both images, replace the original lower-body clothing with the corresponding garments from <Picture 2>. Do not keep the original pants or other clothing from <Picture 1> when replacement garments are available in <Picture 2>.\n\nPreserve the original colors, textures, patterns, materials and distinctive design details of every transferred garment. Do not recolor, redesign or mix the clothing from the two images.\n\nAdapt folds, tension, proportions and occlusion to the pose in <Picture 1>. Preserve the original person's face, hairstyle, body proportions and pose without introducing facial features, body characteristics or background elements from <Picture 2>.\n\nChange clothing only, with natural shadows, seams and realistic fabric integration.\n\nThe final result must show the original person from <Picture 1> wearing the complete visible outfit from <Picture 2>, including both upper-body and lower-body garments wherever they are visible.",
        2048,
        2048
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "prompt": "Edit <Picture 1>. Keep the person EXACTLY the same individual, but dress them in the complete outfit from <Picture 2>.\n\nUse <Picture 1> for the person's facial identity, skin, hair, body shape, original pose, hands, environment and camera composition. Use <Picture 2> ONLY for garments, clothing layers, colors, fabric, materials, patterns, fit and clothing-related accessories.\n\nTransfer the distinctive wardrobe from <Picture 2> accurately rather than inventing an unrelated outfit.\n\nIMPORTANT: Replace the entire visible outfit, not just the upper-body clothing. Transfer all corresponding garments from <Picture 2>, including shirts, tops, sweaters, jackets, coats, pants, jeans, trousers, skirts, dresses, footwear, hats, belts and other clothing accessories when present.\n\nPay particular attention to lower-body clothing. If pants, jeans, skirts or other lower-body garments are visible in both images, replace the original lower-body clothing with the corresponding garments from <Picture 2>. Do not keep the original pants or other clothing from <Picture 1> when replacement garments are available in <Picture 2>.\n\nPreserve the original colors, textures, patterns, materials and distinctive design details of every transferred garment. Do not recolor, redesign or mix the clothing from the two images.\n\nAdapt folds, tension, proportions and occlusion to the pose in <Picture 1>. Preserve the original person's face, hairstyle, body proportions and pose without introducing facial features, body characteristics or background elements from <Picture 2>.\n\nChange clothing only, with natural shadows, seams and realistic fabric integration.\n\nThe final result must show the original person from <Picture 1> wearing the complete visible outfit from <Picture 2>, including both upper-body and lower-body garments wherever they are visible.",
        "width": 2048,
        "height": 2048
      }
    },
